{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"f8f9044ed521d3ea5a92d50399535359cd9b0a0890aed1835d6d6e234ffb994c","digest":{"component_or_area":"attestation signing substrate","key_entities":["src/rebar/attest/","src/rebar/signing.py",".signing-key","REBAR_SIGNING_KEY","DSSE","PAE","ssh-keygen -Y","allowed_signers","SIGNATURE event type","key_id","sign(kind, body_bytes)","verify(kind, envelope, trust_root)","RFC 8725","RFC 8785","securesystemslib","docs/adr/"],"problem_keywords":["asymmetric signing","attestation","dsse envelope","sshsig","pluggable scheme registry","offline verification","alg confusion","fail-closed","domain separation","hmac legacy scheme","per-kind policy table","pae"],"propositions":["rebar signs attestations with symmetric HMAC and needs an asymmetric, verify-by-anyone signing substrate shared by the identity and op-cert epics.","A new attestation module exposes sign/verify where the scheme, namespace, and trust-root are selected from an out-of-band per-kind policy table, never from the envelope.","DSSE PAE is implemented per v1.0.0 so verification operates on exact stored bytes and never re-serializes parsed JSON, closing canonicalization and alg-confusion attack classes.","An SSHSIG scheme signs and verifies offline via ssh-keygen subprocess with argv arrays, branching only on exit code and allowlisting namespace and principal, failing closed on tampered bytes, wrong namespace, unknown principal, substituted key, and expired window.","The existing HMAC signer is registered as a legacy scheme so pre-existing plan-review and completion-verifier attestations still verify unchanged.","ssh-keygen availability and version (>=8.9) is detected and its absence fails closed with no silent pass."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785203250518227708,"uuid":"136b52fa-43fb-49de-bfbc-1486ad231b97"}